    "Simulation is active. ThermalPilot does not control heating.": "Hermun virk. ThermalPilot stýrir ekki hitun.",
    "Observation and learning only; no thermostat control.": "Aðeins mælingar og nám; engin stýring.",
    "ThermalPilot controls thermostat targets.": "ThermalPilot stýrir hitastillimörkum.",
    "Seasonal fallback temperatures are used.": "Árstíðavarahiti notaður.",
    "Scheduled targets remain simulated; season transitions can change thermostat targets.": "Áætlun hermd; árstíðir geta breytt raunmörkum.",
    "Live thermostat control is not enabled.": "Raunstýring ekki virk.",
    "Target changes include the shared start/stop offsets. The temperature forecast models the planned heating period; actual valve and heat-pump delays must be checked against observations.": "Upphafs- og lokahliðrun innifalin. Athuga rauntafír loka og dælu.",
    "These forecasts were saved 1, 3 or 6 hours before the measurements. Later readings do not change them. Lower error is better; compare it with simply predicting no temperature change. Different heating, computers and other heat sources can affect the result.": "Spár vistaðar 1, 3 eða 6 klst fyrr, breytast ekki síðar. Minna frávik betra; bera saman við óbreyttan hita. Annar varmi hefur áhrif.",
    "Compare recorded temperatures with forecasts saved hours earlier. The accuracy cards also compare against predicting no temperature change. Forecasts assume the proposed heating plan; actual heating may differ, especially during simulation.": "Bera saman við eldri spár og óbreyttan hita. Raunhitun getur verið önnur, sérstaklega í hermun.",
    "Forecasts are compared with measurements within five minutes of their due time. “Similar heating” means observed demand matched the forecast for at least 90% of observations, with no large recording gaps. These counts give context, not a guarantee of accuracy.": "Mæling innan fimm mínútna. Svipuð hitun: ≥90% samsvörun án stórra eyða. Fjöldi tryggir ekki nákvæmni.",
    "Each row shows the latest observation within its 15-minute interval, not an average. Suggested thermostat target is the setting ThermalPilot would apply, not a room-temperature forecast. Table shows up to 288 intervals. Original observations remain stored internally. Short chart views use 15-minute time labels; longer views use wider intervals.": "Síðasta mæling á 15 mín, ekki meðaltal. Mark er stilling, ekki spá. Allt að 288 bil; frumgögn geymd.",
    "Suggested On means the boosted target window, including valve timing offsets. Relay On means observed demand; it does not guarantee heat flow.": "Tillaga kveikt er hækkað mark með lokahliðrun. Liði sýnir þörf, tryggir ekki varma.",
    ", without heating, remaining slab warmth or appliance heat. Lower temperature loss means slower modeled cooling. This is a model estimate, not measured energy efficiency or an insulation rating.": ", án hitunar, afgangsvarma eða tækja. Minna tap er hægari reiknuð kólnun; ekki orkumat eða einangrunarmat.",
    "Cooling-speed bands are provisional: under 1 h, 1–2 h, 2–4 h, 4–8 h, and 8 h or longer per 1°C drop. For a selected house type, badges instead compare with that type: under 0.5×, 0.5–0.8×, 0.8–1.25×, 1.25–2×, and at least 2× its reference cooling time. Initial rooms share starting estimates and remain unrated. Comparisons become more useful as their heat-loss parameters adapt to observations. Wind, ventilation, sensor placement and unmeasured heat sources can affect the estimates. The listed time describes this reference test, not how long heating can safely remain off in your home.": "Upphafslíkön eins. Vindur, loftræsting, skynjarar og annar varmi hafa áhrif. Viðmiðunartími er ekki örugg slökkvunarlengd.",
    "Learned parameters and season aggregates are retained when old observations are compacted.": "Lærð gildi og árstíðasummur geymast við þjöppun.",
    "Open a Home Assistant dashboard once, then return here to load embedded history cards.": "Opna Home Assistant-borð og snúa aftur til að hlaða sögu.",
    "Water-based systems only: raise the thermostat target this many minutes before the planned heat-delivery session, allowing slow valves to open. Electric and air distribution ignore this setting and use no advance offset.": "Aðeins vatn: hækka fyrir hæga loka. Rafmagn/loft hunsa hliðrun.",
    "Water-based systems only: lower the thermostat target this many minutes before the planned heat-delivery session ends, allowing valves to close. Electric and air distribution ignore this setting and use no closing offset.": "Aðeins vatn: lækka snemma fyrir lokun. Rafmagn/loft hunsa hliðrun.",
    "What produces heat for your house. Select air-to-water for your water floor system supplied by an air-source heat pump. Gas, oil, wood and district heating need their own fuel-cost logic; choosing a house detail does not yet enable a different controller or reset learned room data.": "Varmagjafi húss. Eldsneyti fær ekki kostnaðarstýringu; herbergisgögn geymd.",
    "How heat reaches rooms: circulating water in floors or radiators, electric floor/ceiling/panels, or warm air. Mixed means different rooms use different systems. Water distribution can optionally use a heating-water sensor and uses valve timing. Electric and warm-air distribution ignore those inputs and learn response from observed thermostat demand. Mixed and Other retain water requirements until room overrides are supported.": "Vatn notar lokatíma og valfrjálsan skynjara. Rafmagn/loft læra þörf. Blandað heldur vatnsstillingum.",
    "The construction around floor heating, which affects how slowly heat is stored and released. Concrete slab describes your heated floor. Choose Not applicable if there is no floor heating. This does not change your configured response lag or erase learned parameters.": "Gólfefni hefur áhrif á geymslu. Á ekki við án gólfhitunar. Breytir ekki töf eða líkani.",
    "The structure below your home: slab on ground, crawl space or basement. A heated concrete floor can be above a basement, so this is separate from Heated floor. Choose Unknown if unsure. This descriptive setting does not reset observation history or learned models.": "Undirstaða aðskilin frá gólfhitun. Velja Óþekkt ef óvíst. Gögn og líkön geymast.",
    "Sunlight through large windows, especially south-facing windows, can warm a room. No additional physical solar heating system is needed. Select the main direction of those windows to enable solar estimates, or Solar heating off to turn them off. Home Assistant’s location determines seasonal sun elevation and azimuth; cloud conditions come from your weather source. The effect starts at zero and learns gradually. Missing sunlight data assumes no solar warmth; room temperature limits still apply.": "Sól um stóra glugga, engin sólarhitakerfi þarf. Stefna, staður og ský gefa sólaráhrif, lærð frá núlli. Vantar gögn: enginn sólarhiti; hitamörk gilda.",
    "Clear means the windows receive direct sunlight without major obstructions. Choose Partly shaded for some trees, buildings or overhangs, or Mostly shaded when sunlight is usually blocked. Forecasts use a more cautious solar allowance: partly shaded uses 65% and mostly shaded 30% of the clear allowance. Actual room warming is still learned from observations; no solar heat is assumed before learning. Seasonal leaf cover and changing shading can still affect accuracy.": "Óskyggt, hálf- eða mikið skyggt: 100%, 65% eða 30% sólaráhrifa. Raunvarmi lærður; skuggi getur breyst.",
    "Optional local wind sensor, for example sensor.netatmo_tuuli_ms using m/s. Valid readings are averaged over the last 30 minutes. ThermalPilot learns a separate wind effect only after enough varied observations; no fixed wind penalty is assumed. Missing, invalid or unchanged-for-two-hours readings are ignored, and normal temperature-based planning and heating continue. Fresh wind correction gradually returns to typical conditions in forecasts further ahead. A stable calm reading may also be ignored conservatively. Units are detected automatically.": "Valfrjáls vindur, sjálfvirkar einingar, 30 mín meðaltal. Áhrif lærð úr breytilegum gögnum. Vantar, ógilt eða óbreytt 2 klst hunsað; venjuleg hitun heldur áfram. Langspár nálgast venjulegan vind.",
    "Emergency lower temperature limit shared by all rooms. Each room’s own target is the normal comfort goal. ThermalPilot prioritizes avoiding this limit even when electricity is expensive; this value is not the idle thermostat target.": "Algjört lágmark, ekki hvíldarmark. Herbergismark er þægindi; mörk varin á dýrum tímum.",
    "Upper temperature limit shared by all rooms. Extra heating and heat storage must stay within this limit.": "Hámark fyrir öll herbergi; aukinn varmi má ekki fara yfir.",
    "Optional sensor with forecast timestamp/value entries, such as Nordpool Predict FI. Only relative expensive/cheap patterns after confirmed prices are used, so no forecast price unit or additional costs are required. The Source price unit setting applies only to the confirmed total-price sensor. An expensive upcoming period can increase the heat reserve at the end of the known-price plan. Forecast prices are not compared directly with your total prices, used as confirmed prices or used to execute future heating commands. Missing forecasts keep normal planning. Confirmed prices always determine the executable schedule.": "Valfrjáls hlutfallsleg verðspá eftir staðfest verð. Einingar/aukakostnaður óþarfir. Getur aukið forða, aldrei staðfest verð eða bein framtíðarstýring. Vantar: venjuleg áætlun.",
    "Notify in Home Assistant when a room temperature sensor stays unchanged or unavailable for this many hours. A stable room can also have an unchanged reading, so the warning asks you to check the sensor. ThermalPilot sends at most one sensor notification per calendar day. Monitoring runs while ThermalPilot is active; long monitoring gaps restart the timer.": "Vara við eftir þennan tíma án nýs herbergishita.",
    "Summer fallback always applies from 15.5. through 30.9. Outside those dates, it also applies when the day’s lowest forecast temperature is equal to or above this value. For example, a setting of 6°C means the daily minimum must be at least 6°C for ThermalPilot to use summer fallback temperatures. Lower readings already observed that day are included. If a full-day forecast is unavailable outside the summer dates, winter fallback is used.": "Sumarvarahiti 15.5.–30.9., annars ef lágmark dags nær mörkum. Vantar spá virkjar ekki sumar utan dagsetninga.",
    "Negative values reduce estimated heat loss while the fireplace is active; −20% means a 20% reduction.": "Neikvætt lækkar tap við virkan arin; −20% er 20% minna.",
    "Prefer a sensor that includes electricity prices and additional costs, such as VAT, transfer tariffs, electricity tax and retailer margin. A variable electricity-price sensor without these costs also works. If transfer tariffs differ between day and night, including them helps ThermalPilot choose the cheapest heating hours; omitting them can shift heating to hours that are less economical overall. Select a source containing today/tomorrow or timestamped raw_today/raw_tomorrow price lists, and choose the matching source price unit.": "Helst heildarverð með sköttum, flutningi og álagi. Breytilegt verð eitt virkar; mismunandi dag/næturflutningur getur skekkt val tíma. Nota today/tomorrow eða tímasett raw_today/raw_tomorrow með réttri einingu.",
    "Hourly average uses fixed hourly averages of the source prices. 15 minutes plans using quarter-hour intervals. Flexible builds heating sessions in 15-minute steps, allowing runs such as 60 or 75 minutes while respecting the minimum flexible heating run.": "Klst meðaltal, 15 mín bil eða sveigjanlegt í 15 mín skrefum með lágmarki.",
    "The shortest planned heating session in flexible scheduling mode. Longer sessions can be chosen in 15-minute steps. This setting applies to flexible runs; valve opening and closing offsets are applied separately.": "Stysta sveigjanleg lota; lengri í 15 mín skrefum.",
    "Initial estimate of how slowly heat input affects room temperature and how long its effect persists. Concrete slabs often need a longer delay, but lightweight floors, radiators, electric heaters and air systems also have a response time. Use a shorter value for faster systems. This remains relevant to every distribution; it is separate from valve opening or closing time.": "Upphafsmat tregðu og afgangsvarma; líkan lærir raunviðbrögð.",
    "The warm outdoor endpoint of the initial heating-hours curve. At this temperature or warmer, the starting model assumes the lower daily heating need. This curve seeds the model before enough real heating and cooling observations are available.": "Hlýtt upphafsmark daglegrar þörfar; raunviðbrögð lærð.",
    "The cold outdoor endpoint of the initial heating-hours curve. At this temperature or colder, the starting model assumes the higher daily heating need. Set it below the warm endpoint. Actual room response is learned from observations.": "Kalt upphafsmark, lægra en hlýtt; raunviðbrögð lærð.",
    "Allows real thermostat setpoint changes when ThermalPilot changes between Active and Passive. Active applies each room’s target temperature; Passive applies the seasonal fallback: the shared summer setpoint or each room’s normal target in winter. These commands can occur even with simulation enabled. This does not enable live heating schedule control.": "Raunárstíðaskipti líka í hermun. Virkt: herbergismark; óvirkt: sumar/vetrarvarahiti. Ekki áætlunarstýring.",
    "The thermostat target used for all configured rooms while ThermalPilot is Passive, if real Active/Passive season setpoint control is enabled. A low summer target normally prevents heating without switching off the thermostats.": "Sameiginlegt sumarmark í óvirku með árstíðastýringu. Lágt mark hindrar hitun án þess að slökkva á hitastillum.",
    "Degrees added to each room’s target temperature during a suggested heating window. For example, a 20 °C target with a 1.5 °C boost suggests a 21.5 °C thermostat setpoint to store heat. Scheduled targets remain simulated in this version.": "Gráður yfir herbergismarki fyrir geymslu, t.d. 20 + 1,5 = 21,5°C.",
    "Negative values temporarily lower the thermostat target during expensive electricity hours. After a planned heating session, ThermalPilot first restores the room’s normal target. It then chooses reduction only when predicted stored warmth can avoid thermostat heating while supporting room comfort. For example, −1°C allows a 20°C target to be reduced to 19°C during selected costly hours. The reduced target never goes below Minimum allowed temperature. Normal target is restored when reduction is no longer useful; a new planned heating session uses the boosted target. Duration is chosen by the plan, not a fixed number of hours.": "Neikvæð lækkun á dýrum stundum við nægan forða. Fyrst venjulegt eftir lotu, aldrei undir lágmarki. Endurheimt þegar óþörf; tími frá áætlun.",
    "Select the measured supply-water temperature. A temperature sensor uses its state; a climate entity uses its current_temperature attribute. This is the measured water temperature, not the thermostat’s target. Optional for water-based systems. A valid reading adjusts the estimated heating output. Without it, planning and learning continue from observed thermostat demand, without a water-temperature adjustment. Missing readings do not force fallback targets.": "Valfrjáls mældur framrennslishiti; climate notar current_temperature, ekki mark. Leiðréttir afl. Vantar stöðvar ekki nám/áætlun né varahita.",
    "Simulation calculates heating suggestions without applying scheduled targets. Disable simulation and confirm to enable real thermostat control. If another automation controls these thermostats, disable it first. Observation and learning continue in both modes.": "Hermun notar ekki áætluð mörk. Slökkva og staðfesta fyrir raunstýringu; slökkva á annarri tengdri sjálfvirkni ef til. Nám í báðum hömum.",
    "Choose the interface language. Room and entity names remain unchanged. Save settings to keep the choice. Embedded history cards follow this choice where supported by Home Assistant.": "Velja tungumál og vista. Heiti haldast. Innbyggð saga fylgir þar sem stutt.",
    "All room timelines share the price chart’s time axis.${zones.length?' Zone rows show recorded heating and cooling only; off and standby periods stay empty. Plan adds suggested heating only for tariff-optimized zones.':''} Teal shows the suggested thermostat boost window; amber shows observed heating demand. ": "Sameiginlegur tímaás. Blágrænt: hækkun; appelsínugult: mæld þörf. ",
    "The selected period controls past history. Today and tomorrow are included when prices are published. Recorded activity is shown before now; future suggestions follow the current plan. Price gaps stay empty. ": "Tímabil velur sögu; í dag/á morgun með verði. Fyrir nú mælingar; eftir nú áætlun. Verðeyður tómar. ",
    "Times align to 15-minute boundaries; wider views show fewer labels. Hover, focus or tap a price bar or heating period for details.": "15 mín mörk; löng sýn færri merkingar. Benda, velja eða snerta fyrir nánar.",
    "This measures initial data collection, not model trustworthiness. Continue validating forecasts and heating suggestions before enabling live control. Learning continues after initial data collection.": "Upphafssöfnun er ekki áreiðanleiki. Meta tillögur fyrir raunstýringu; nám heldur áfram.",
    "History collection and learning paused because outdoor temperature is unavailable. Existing model parameters are retained.": "Saga og nám í bið án útihita. Líkan helst.",
    "No weather forecast: current outdoor temperature is held constant.": "Engin veðurspá; núverandi útihiti fastur.",
    "Live control awaits confirmation. Enable simulation, save, then disable it and confirm to activate thermostat control.": "Stýring bíður staðfestingar. Hermun á, vista, svo af og staðfesta.",
    "Waiting for enough heating and idle observations to estimate the remaining time.": "Bíð eftir fleiri hitunar- og hvíldarmælingum fyrir tímamat.",
    "A door/window contact sensor can monitor the fireplace damper position. Select the sensor state that means the fireplace is in use. For a damper contact sensor, Open normally means active and Closed means inactive. Door/window labels are converted to Home Assistant’s underlying on/off values. Other sensors show their declared options, current valid state and any saved value. A contact state indicates the damper position; it does not prove that a fire is burning.": "Hurða/gluggaskynjari á reykspjaldi: Opið oft virkt, Lokað óvirkt. Vistað on/off. Aðrir sýna valkosti. Staða sannar ekki brennandi eld.",
